I had someone tell me once: "They'd count the police horses if they could."

&amp;nbsp;

Penn State's Pinstripe Bowl win over Boston College had a higher attendance than Derek Jeter's final game, for similar reasons, as the football roster and support staff is larger than baseball. I like to remind my Yankees fan friend this detail often.

Pretend you don't like Michigan or Ohio State. Their standing in the conference doesn't have any impact on your team. You're a Boise State fan. It's the Saturday after Thanksgiving. You sit down with a bowl of turkey and get ready to watch one of the biggest games on the entire calendar.  You don't want a game that seems determined from the beginning, as the results have shown lately. 

&amp;nbsp;

Now, granted, many of these games have come down to the wire... But this year especially wasn't very fun for me to watch. I was really expecting to watch an invigorated Michigan defense really play a stellar game against Ohio State. What we got was "more of the same," which is a quote from a friend that's very into college football. I'm looking forward to the next time Michigan wins, because it will be a huge shot in the arm to the rivalry.
